<?xml version="1.0"?>


<!DOCTYPE rdf:RDF [
    <!ENTITY terms "http://purl.org/dc/terms/" >
    <!ENTITY owl "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" >
    <!ENTITY swrl "http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#" >
    <!ENTITY dc "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" >
    <!ENTITY swrlb "http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrlb#" >
    <!ENTITY arto "http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#" >
    <!ENTITY xsd "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" >
    <!ENTITY skos "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" >
    <!ENTITY rdfs "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" >
    <!ENTITY rdf "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" >
]>


<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto/merged#"
     xml:base="http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto/merged"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:swrl="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#"
     xmlns:terms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:swrlb="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrlb#"
     xmlns:arto="http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto/merged">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Pilot Individuals</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Step 2</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Step 3</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Step 4</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Step 5</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M2 Traceability Module</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M3 Sprint Module</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO M4 Semantic Resolution Module</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO — Agile Requirements Traceability Ontology</rdfs:label>
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="&xsd;gYear">2026</terms:created>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.1.0 — step 5 final: MaintenanceArtefact + Sprint + SKOS. v1.1.0: skos:exactMatch/closeMatch declared as object properties (previously read as annotations by Protégé 4.3, which blocked SWRL R3); duplicate Improvement exactMatch EnhancementRequest removed (kept in M4)</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0 — step 4: DesignArtefact + DeploymentArtefact + Event ODP + RT properties</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.2.0 — rule and SKOS documentation aligned with executable rules (R1–R2 in M2, R3 in M4, run by HermiT in Protégé 4.3); R4 documentation only; OrphanArtefact two-way; SKOS counts corrected. 1.1.0 — fabricated IRIs removed · ODP imports removed · honest reuse documentation</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>5.2.0 — skos:exactMatch declared as object property so pilot exactMatch triples are read as object property assertions (required for SWRL R3); link_005 comment corrected</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.1.0 — step 2: RT object properties + OrphanArtefact. v1.1.0: OrphanArtefact rewritten as AgileArtefact and not (hasTraceLink some Thing) and not (inverse hasTraceLink some Thing), for OWL 2 DL compliance and to cover incoming as well as outgoing links; IrreflexiveProperty restored on duplicates; hasPart rationale corrected. v1.2.0: reportedIn not populated from TAWOS (no explicit source; type-pair assertion would create false traces); hasImplementingTask restricted to Associative and Structural Story→Task/Sub-task links (338).</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0 — step 3: TestingArtefact + CodeCommit + deferred RT properties</owl:versionInfo>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Artefact Module — Step 2: Core RT object properties and OrphanArtefact classifier.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Artefact Module — Step 5 (FINAL): MaintenanceArtefact, DefectArtefact migration, full Sprint module, documents and addresses RT properties, M4 SKOS semantic resolution preview.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M2 Traceability Module — TraceLink hierarchy, TraceLinkType controlled vocabulary (7 semantic clusters), SDLC link direction, and executable SWRL rules R1 (impact inference) and R2 (test coverage). R3 is executable in M4; R4 is documentation only. Covers CQ3, CQ4, CQ5, CQ6, CQ7, CQ8.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M4 Semantic Resolution Module — TermVariant, SynonymCluster, DriftEvent, SKOS synonym mappings, and SWRL Rule R3 for cross-sprint semantic equivalence propagation (CQ8).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">Agile Requirements Traceability Ontology — a modular OWL-DL network for formally representing and querying traceability links across Agile software artefacts. Built on the TAWOS dataset (39 real Agile projects, 456,000+ issues). PhD research, University of Botswana, 2026.</dc:description>
        <dc:creator>Tshepho Koboyatshwene</dc:creator>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.2.0 — M2: TraceLink + TraceLinkType + executable SWRL R1a–R1e, R2a–R2b; cluster volumes audited OUTBOUND-only; R1e added (Nov 2026)</owl:versionInfo>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M3 Sprint Module — SprintBacklog, BacklogItem, sprint performance metrics (velocity, throughput, sprintGoal), component data property, and sprint bridge properties.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:contributor>University of Botswana</dc:contributor>
        <dc:subject>Requirements Traceability · Agile Software Development · OWL-DL · TAWOS · NeOn · METHONTOLOGY</dc:subject>
        <owl:versionInfo>0.6.0 — middle-out step 1 v5: SDLC-aligned hierarchy, no UnclassifiedIssue</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.1.0 — M4: TermVariant + SynonymCluster + DriftEvent + SKOS (exactMatch/closeMatch as object properties) + executable R3a/R3b/R3c</owl:versionInfo>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Artefact Module — Step 3: TestingArtefact (TestCase, TestResult), CodeCommit, and deferred RT properties (verifies, fixes, derives, supersedes, tracesTo).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO M1 Artefact Module — Step 4: DesignArtefact, DeploymentArtefact, Event ODP (Sprint), PartOf ODP formal annotation, and new RT properties (refines, realizes, fixedIn, affectedIn, containedIn).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Agile Requirements Traceability Ontology. University of Botswana PhD Research. Candidate: Tshepho Koboyatshwene.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Consolidated pilot individuals for smoke testing CQ1–CQ5 and CQ-D1–CQ-D4. All cross-step RT assertions declared here to avoid Protégé SPARQL import chain issues.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Root ontology for the ARTO network. Imports all four modules (M1 Artefact · M2 Traceability · M3 Sprint · M4 Semantic Resolution) and declares five bridge axioms connecting the modules. S3 reuse of ontological resources (Lapeña 2019 · Pakdeetrakulwong 2015) documented honestly as intent not executed due to OWL file unavailability. S7 ODP reuse documented at conceptual instantiation level with rdfs:isDefinedBy citations in module files. Licence: all rights reserved — this ontology is unpublished PhD research (University of Botswana, 2026) and is not licensed for reuse or redistribution pending examination and the author&apos;s decision on a formal publication licence; see dct:license.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:rights>University of Botswana PhD Research — Tshepho Koboyatshwene 2026</dc:rights>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0 — M3: SprintBacklog + BacklogItem + metrics + bridge properties</owl:versionInfo>
        <terms:license rdf:resource="http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto/LICENCE"/>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Object Properties
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#addresses -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;addresses">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">addresses</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AgileArtefact (typically UserStory or SprintTask) addresses a maintenance concern (SupportRequest or ProblemTicket). TAWOS: Addresses link type (22 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric. An ARTO-specific extension beyond the four verified Ramesh and Jarke (2001) categories — no corresponding named sub-type is claimed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#affectedIn -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;affectedIn">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">affected in</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AgileArtefact (typically Bug) was discovered or reported in a specific Version. TAWOS: Affected_Version junction table, 264,004 total rows (verified via direct COUNT, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric. Highest-volume RT property in the entire TAWOS dataset. Maps from Affected_Version.Affected_Version_ID → Version.ID.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#affectsArtefact -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;affectsArtefact">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">affects artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a DriftEvent to the AgileArtefact whose title changed. Functional — each DriftEvent affects exactly one AgileArtefact. TAWOS: Change_Log.Issue_ID → AgileArtefact individual.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#belongsToSprint -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;belongsToSprint">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">belongs to sprint</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a UserStory or SprintTask to the Sprint it is assigned to. TAWOS: Issue.Sprint_ID (Int) foreign key. Functional — TAWOS records a single Sprint_ID per issue, so an artefact has at most one belongsToSprint assertion; carry-over across sprints is represented through BacklogItems (an artefact can appear as a BacklogItem in several sprints), not through additional belongsToSprint assertions. Core M3 bridge property enabling CQ1 sprint context queries and CQ7 sprint velocity analysis. Deliberately NOT a subproperty of hasTraceLink: sprint membership is not a trace link between artefacts, and because hasTraceLink has range AgileArtefact, a subproperty ranging over Sprint would entail that every Sprint is an AgileArtefact, contradicting Sprint&apos;s position under Event, outside the AgileArtefact subtree.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#blocks -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;blocks">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">blocks</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One artefact prevents progress on another. TAWOS: Blocks/Blockers/Blocker/Block/Blocked (9169 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric and Irreflexive.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#causes -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;causes">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">causes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bug causes or introduces another artefact. TAWOS: Cause/Caused (1444 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). The raw Jira label Regression is reassigned to verifies (Oct 2026) — it is a test-relationship synonym, not a causation link; the figure above excludes it. Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Domain restricted to Bug — all causation links in TAWOS originate from Bug individuals.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#containedIn -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;containedIn">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contained in</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AgileArtefact is grouped within a Version milestone. TAWOS: 0 links within this dataset (verified via direct COUNT, Oct 2026 audit — no &apos;Containment&apos;-named link in TAWOS targets a Milestone-typed Version; an earlier, unverified estimate of 55 is superseded). Retained as a declared property for other datasets and for CQ-D2, which was verified against hand-curated pilot sample individuals rather than bulk TAWOS extraction. Asymmetric. Domain: AgileArtefact. Range: Version (versionType = Milestone).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#contains -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;contains">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contains</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:containedIn. A Version (milestone) contains one or more AgileArtefacts. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;containedIn"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#dependsOn -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;dependsOn">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">depends on</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Prerequisite dependency between artefacts. TAWOS: Depends/Dependency/Depend/dependent/Required (9763 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#derives -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;derives">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">derives</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One artefact is derived from another through refinement or splitting. TAWOS: Derived/Issue split/Split (570 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Echoes the Evolution category of Ramesh and Jarke (2001) rather than a specific named sub-type. Common pattern: large UserStory split into smaller stories (Issue split).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#documents -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;documents">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">documents</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Documentation artefact formally describes or explains another AgileArtefact. TAWOS: Reference/Duplicate/Relates links between Documentation and Bug/Story/Improvement (5 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit; supersedes an earlier estimate of 114 that double-counted both link directions). Asymmetric. An ARTO-specific extension beyond the four verified Ramesh and Jarke (2001) categories (Chapter 6, Section 6.5) — no corresponding named sub-type in their taxonomy is claimed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Documentation"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#duplicates -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;duplicates">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;SymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">duplicates</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Marks two artefacts as duplicates. TAWOS: Duplicate (29456 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). The raw Jira label Cloners (7,561 rows) is deliberately excluded: clone-provenance is administrative content-copy metadata, not a traceability relationship. Symmetric and Irreflexive. Irreflexivity was briefly removed and then restored (v1.1.0): the property is simple, so OWL 2 DL permits it, and TAWOS contains no Duplicate link from an issue to itself (0 rows).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#fixedIn -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;fixedIn">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fixed in</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AgileArtefact (typically Bug or SprintTask) was resolved in a specific Version. TAWOS: Fix_Version junction table, 224,254 total rows (verified via direct COUNT, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric. Highest-volume deployment RT property in TAWOS. Maps directly from Fix_Version.Fixed_Version_ID → Version.ID.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#fixes -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;fixes">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fixes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An ImplementationArtefact (SprintTask or CodeCommit) fixes a Bug. TAWOS: Fixes/Resolve (130 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Connects ImplementationArtefact to DefectArtefact — closes the defect traceability loop in the RT chain.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#follows -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;follows">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">follows</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AgileArtefact sequentially follows another AgileArtefact (temporal/logical precedence, distinct from blocks — no hard dependency implied). TAWOS: Follows link type (25 links). Asymmetric. An ARTO-specific extension beyond the four verified Ramesh and Jarke (2001) categories — no corresponding named sub-type is claimed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#followsSprint -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;followsSprint">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">follows sprint</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a Sprint to the Sprint that immediately preceded it within the same project: &apos;B followsSprint A&apos; means A is the earlier sprint. TAWOS: derived from Sprint.Start_Date ordering WHERE Project_ID = same AND Start_Date IS NOT NULL. Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Enables sprint sequence analysis and multi-sprint velocity trend queries for CQ7.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasAffected -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasAffected">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has affected</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:affectedIn. A Version has one or more AgileArtefacts discovered in it. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;affectedIn"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasBacklog -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasBacklog">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has backlog</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a Sprint to its SprintBacklog. Functional — each Sprint has exactly one SprintBacklog. Core M3 bridge property connecting sprint lifecycle to backlog content.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasBacklogItem -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasBacklogItem">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has backlog item</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a SprintBacklog to its constituent BacklogItems. One-to-many — a backlog contains multiple items. Core M3 content property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasFixFor -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasFixFor">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has fix for</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:fixedIn. A Version has a fix for one or more AgileArtefacts. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;fixedIn"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasImplementingTask -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasImplementingTask">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has implementing task</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Decomposes a UserStory into SprintTasks. TAWOS: asserted on Story→Task/Sub-task links whose raw name maps to the Associative or Structural cluster (relatesTo, references, supersedes, hasPart, hasStory): 338 links, OUTBOUND-only, Nov 2026. Duplicate, blocking/dependency and Issue split links between the same types (143) are excluded because they do not express implementation. TAWOS has no parent-issue column, so issue links are the only source. Asymmetric. Core CQ1 property; feeds SWRL R1a and R1b. Part of decomposition chain: Epic → UserStory → SprintTask.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasLinkType -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasLinkType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has link type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The semantic cluster this TraceLink belongs to. Points to one of the 7 TraceLinkType named individuals. Functional — each link belongs to exactly one semantic cluster. Core CQ7 property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasMember -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasMember">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has member</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:belongsToSprint. A Sprint has one or more AgileArtefact members. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;belongsToSprint"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasPart -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasPart">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has part</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Compositional containment — one artefact contains another. TAWOS: Part/Child-Issue/Children/Includes/Containment/Container/Incorporates (3088 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit; includes all &apos;Containment&apos;-named rows, none of which target a Milestone-typed Version in this dataset — see containedIn in Step 4 for the distinction). Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Implements PartOf Content ODP. Note: SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink only. SubPropertyOf relatesTo was removed for a semantic reason: relatesTo is Symmetric, so the axiom would make every part also relate to its whole in both directions, hiding the direction of composition. hasPart is not transitive, so it is simple in OWL 2 DL either way.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Formally instantiates PartOf Content ODP (S7). Source: http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/partof.owl. ARTO instantiation: AgileArtefact plays both Part and Whole roles — UserStory hasPart SprintTask (via hasImplementingTask), Suggestion hasPart SubSuggestion. Re-declared here with formal ODP annotation — property axioms defined in Step 2.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/partof.owl"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasReportedBug -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasReportedBug">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has reported bug</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:reportedIn. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;reportedIn"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasSourceArtefact -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasSourceArtefact">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has source artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The AgileArtefact from which this TraceLink originates. Functional — each TraceLink has exactly one source.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasStory -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasStory">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has story</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links an Epic to its constituent UserStories. TAWOS: Epic Story, 173 links (verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT, Oct 2026 audit; Parent Feature is mapped to hasPart instead, not hasStory, per the finalized raw-link-type mapping). Asymmetric. Clustered under StructuralLink_Type. Sits above hasImplementingTask: Epic → UserStory → SprintTask.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Epic"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasTargetArtefact -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasTargetArtefact">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has target artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The AgileArtefact to which this TraceLink points. Functional — each TraceLink has exactly one target.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasTermVariant -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasTermVariant">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has term variant</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:refersToIssue. An AgileArtefact can have multiple TermVariant labels across projects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;refersToIssue"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasTraceLink -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasTraceLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has trace link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">General trace link superproperty. All specific RT properties are SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink. Used in the definition of OrphanArtefact. Not simple in OWL 2 DL, because the transitive property impacts (M2) is a subproperty, so no cardinality restriction may be placed on it. Bridges M1 and M2 in the full ARTO network.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">S3 REUSE INTENT (not executed) — NeOn scenario S3, reuse of ontological resources:
arto:hasTraceLink was designed with Pakdeetrakulwong et al. (2015) in view —
An Ontology-Based Multi-Agent System to Support Requirements Traceability in
Multi-Site Software Development Environment. Proceedings of the ASWEC 2015
24th Australasian Software Engineering Conference, Vol. II, pp. 96-100. ACM.
DOI: 10.1145/2811681.2811700.

CORRECTION (Oct 2026): an earlier version of this annotation described a
TraceLink concept in that paper, cited it under a different title and venue
(International Journal of Software Engineering and Its Applications, Vol 9(2)),
and recorded an intended bridge axiom arto:TraceLink owl:equivalentClass
pakdee:TraceLink. Neither the title/venue nor the TraceLink concept matches the
ASWEC 2015 paper cited in this thesis. That paper defines no TraceLink class: it
layers three requirement-interdependency relations (Requires, Refines,
Conflicts_with), adapted from Dahlstedt and Persson, and a table of change-impact
rules on the Software Engineering Ontology of Wongthongtham et al. (2009). No
bridge axiom was therefore possible, and none is declared.

The paper&apos;s ontology OWL file was also not publicly available at implementation
time (same barrier as noted on arto:AgileArtefact below). The alignment is
preserved here via this rdfs:comment annotation only. What ARTO shares with the
paper is the purpose of change-impact analysis over linked artefacts: its impact
rules anticipate, in simplified form, ARTO&apos;s arto:impacts property (derived
by SWRL rule R1 and extended by its owl:TransitiveProperty declaration).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasVariant -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasVariant">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has variant</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a SynonymCluster to its constituent TermVariant individuals. One-to-many — a cluster contains at least 2 variants. Core M4 property enabling CQ8 synonym resolution.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SynonymCluster"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#impacts -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;impacts">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;TransitiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">impacts</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Transitive impact property inferred by SWRL Rule R1. If a UserStory has an implementing SprintTask that traces to a CodeCommit, then the UserStory impacts the CodeCommit. Transitive: if A impacts B and B impacts C then A impacts C. SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink — all inferred impact links count in CQ5 coverage queries. Not directly asserted in ETL — produced by HermiT SWRL reasoning.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#inBacklog -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;inBacklog">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in backlog</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:hasBacklogItem. Each BacklogItem belongs to one SprintBacklog.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasBacklogItem"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#inCluster -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;inCluster">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in cluster</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:hasVariant. Each TermVariant belongs to exactly one SynonymCluster. Functional.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;SynonymCluster"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasVariant"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isAddressedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isAddressedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is addressed by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:addresses. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;addresses"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isBacklogOf -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isBacklogOf">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is backlog of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:hasBacklog. Each SprintBacklog belongs to exactly one Sprint. Functional.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasBacklog"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isBlockedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isBlockedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is blocked by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:blocks. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;blocks"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isCausedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isCausedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is caused by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:causes. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;causes"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isDependedOnBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isDependedOnBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is depended on by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:dependsOn. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;dependsOn"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isDerivedFrom -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isDerivedFrom">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is derived from</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:derives. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;derives"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isDocumentedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isDocumentedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is documented by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:documents. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Documentation"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;documents"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isFixedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isFixedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is fixed by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:fixes. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;fixes"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isFollowedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isFollowedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is followed by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:follows. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;follows"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isImpactedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isImpactedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is impacted by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:impacts. Inferred by HermiT.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;impacts"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isImplementedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isImplementedBy">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is implemented by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:hasImplementingTask. A SprintTask implements at least one UserStory.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasImplementingTask"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isPartOf -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isPartOf">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is part of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:hasPart. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasPart"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isRealizedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isRealizedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is realized by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:realizes. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;realizes"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isRefinedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isRefinedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is refined by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:refines. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;refines"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isRelatedTraceLink -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isRelatedTraceLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is related trace link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links related TraceLink individuals e.g. an InferredLink to the AssertedLinks that triggered its inference. Supports CQ6 provenance queries.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isRepresentedAs -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isRepresentedAs">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is represented as</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:refersToArtefact. An AgileArtefact can be represented as a BacklogItem in multiple sprints (if carried over).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;refersToArtefact"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isStoryOf -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isStoryOf">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is story of</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:hasStory. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Epic"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasStory"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isSupersededBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isSupersededBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is superseded by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:supersedes. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;supersedes"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isTracedFrom -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isTracedFrom">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is traced from</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:tracesTo. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;tracesTo"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isVerifiedBy -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;isVerifiedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is verified by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:verifies. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;TestCase"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;verifies"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#precedesSprint -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;precedesSprint">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">precedes sprint</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inverse of arto:followsSprint: &apos;A precedesSprint B&apos; means B follows A, i.e. A is the earlier sprint. Inferred by HermiT — not asserted in ETL. Named precedesSprint rather than isFollowedBy because isFollowedBy is already the inverse of arto:follows.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;followsSprint"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#realizes -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;realizes">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">realizes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An ImplementationArtefact realizes a DesignArtefact by providing a concrete implementation. Literature-grounded, echoing the Satisfaction category of Ramesh and Jarke (2001) rather than a specific named sub-type. TAWOS: Implements (11 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT, Oct 2026 audit; Completes is excluded as an unrelated label). Asymmetric. Distinct from tracesTo (CodeCommit→SprintTask) — realizes captures the higher-level design-to-implementation RT link.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#references -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;references">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;SymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">references</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Explicit citation or pointer between artefacts. TAWOS: Reference (19914 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). Symmetric.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#refersToArtefact -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;refersToArtefact">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">refers to artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a BacklogItem to the AgileArtefact it represents in the sprint context. Functional — each BacklogItem refers to exactly one AgileArtefact. Core M1-M3 bridge: BacklogItem(M3) → AgileArtefact(M1). Enables CQ1 sprint decomposition queries: which UserStories are in sprint X?</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#refersToIssue -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;refersToIssue">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">refers to issue</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a TermVariant to the AgileArtefact individual it labels. Functional — each TermVariant labels exactly one AgileArtefact. Core M4-M1 bridge: TermVariant(M4) → AgileArtefact(M1).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#refines -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;refines">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">refines</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A DesignArtefact refines a RequirementsArtefact by adding implementation detail. Literature-grounded, echoing the Satisfaction category of Ramesh and Jarke (2001) rather than a specific named sub-type. Zero TAWOS occurrences — waterfall-era link type absent from Jira-based Agile projects. Excluded from TAWOS Part 9 evaluation. Included for conceptual completeness and multi-dataset comparability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#relatesTo -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;relatesTo">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;SymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">relates to</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">General associative RT link between any two artefacts. TAWOS: Relates/Related/Relate, plus the catch-all labels Detail and Problem/Incident (37265 links total, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit; supersedes an earlier estimate that double-counted both link directions). Symmetric. Backbone of the TAWOS RT chain — present across all artefact type pairs.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#reportedIn -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;reportedIn">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reported in</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a Bug to the UserStory in which it was discovered. Not populated from TAWOS: the dataset records no explicit reported-in link, and its 1,261 Bug→Story links are mostly Relates, Blocks and Duplicate, so asserting reportedIn on them would create false traces. Used in the pilot data and kept for datasets that record this relationship. Asymmetric. Feeds SWRL R1c (CQ4), which therefore fires on the pilot only. On TAWOS, CQ2 is answered by any hasTraceLink between a Bug and a UserStory.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#supersedes -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;supersedes">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supersedes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One artefact replaces or obsoletes another. TAWOS: Supersession/Supercedes/Supersede (600 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit). Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Adopted mechanism for RequirementCandidate→UserStory promotion — a Suggestion/Improvement/NewFeature superseded by a UserStory documents the acceptance decision trail without reclassifying the original individual (see arto:isAccepted in Step 1 for the disjointness rationale).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#tracesTo -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;tracesTo">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">traces to</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A CodeCommit traces to the SprintTask it implements. Literature-grounded, echoing the Satisfaction category of Ramesh and Jarke (2001) rather than a specific named sub-type. TAWOS bridge: Pull_Request_URL on 646 issues connects to code level. Asymmetric. Completes the RT chain: Epic → UserStory → SprintTask ← CodeCommit.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#triggeredDrift -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;triggeredDrift">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">triggered drift</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a TermVariant to DriftEvent individuals it participated in. A TermVariant triggers a drift when its rawLabel changes (from=old variant, to=new variant).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#verifies -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&arto;verifies">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;AsymmetricProperty"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;IrreflexiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">verifies</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A TestCase verifies a UserStory, SprintTask or Bug. TAWOS: Tested/QA Test/Bonfire Testing/Regression (5426 links, verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit; Regression is included here, reassigned from an earlier, incorrect grouping with causes — it is a test-relationship synonym, not a defect-causation link). Asymmetric and Irreflexive. Core CQ3 property — stories with no incoming verifies link are test coverage gaps. Domain restricted to TestCase.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestCase"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&skos;closeMatch">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">close match</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SKOS mapping property, declared locally as an object property for consistency with skos:exactMatch. Approximate synonym. Not used by any SWRL rule: close matches do not propagate trace links.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="&skos;exactMatch">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">exact match</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SKOS mapping property, declared locally as an object property so SWRL Rule R3 can use it. Strict synonym: same concept, different label. Not declared symmetric or transitive; R3b supplies the backward direction.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Data properties
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TraceLinkType_label -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;TraceLinkType_label">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">type label</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Human-readable label for this TraceLinkType cluster.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TraceLinkType_properties -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;TraceLinkType_properties">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">covered properties</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Comma-separated list of arto: RT properties covered by this TraceLinkType cluster.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TraceLinkType_tawosVolume -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;TraceLinkType_tawosVolume">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TAWOS volume</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Total number of TAWOS Issue_Links rows mapped to this TraceLinkType cluster. Grounded in Query 4 results.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#acceptanceCriteria -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;acceptanceCriteria">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">acceptance criteria</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Description_Code (Text). Conditions for story acceptance.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#activatedDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;activatedDate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">activated date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.Activated_Date (DateTime). When the sprint was formally started. NULL for some sprints — optional property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#affectedUsers -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;affectedUsers">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">affected users</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Number of users affected by this support issue. Literature-grounded. Higher values signal higher priority for bug traceability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SupportRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#approvalDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;approvalDate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">approval date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Date when this design artefact was formally approved. Literature-grounded.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#approvedBy -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;approvedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">approved by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ID of the reviewer or architect who approved this design artefact. Literature-grounded. Connects to Developer/Agent when M3 is built.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#assertionMethod -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;assertionMethod">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">assertion method</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">How this TraceLink was created. Values: ETL (from TAWOS Issue_Links), SWRL (HermiT inferred), Manual (human-asserted). Core CQ6 property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#assigneeId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;assigneeId">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">assignee ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Assignee_ID (Int). Foreign key to User table. Preserves agent assignment information without requiring Agent class individuals — User table has only ID and Project_ID, no name or role data. AgentRole ODP dropped: role cannot be determined from TAWOS data.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#authorId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;authorId">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">author ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The developer who authored this commit. Literature-grounded. Connects to Developer/Agent individuals in M3 via AgentRole ODP. Forward-compatible: pending Git integration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#backlogId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;backlogId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">backlog ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unique identifier for this SprintBacklog. Derived by ETL: Sprint.ID used as backlog ID since each sprint has exactly one backlog. One-to-one relationship with Sprint.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#backlogItemOrder -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;backlogItemOrder">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">backlog item order</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The priority ordering of this BacklogItem within its SprintBacklog. TAWOS: derived from Issue.Priority field (Highest=1, High=2, Medium=3, Low=4, Lowest=5). Supports sprint planning analysis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#backlogSize -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;backlogSize">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">backlog size</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Total number of BacklogItems in this SprintBacklog at sprint start. TAWOS: COUNT(Issue WHERE Sprint_ID = s.ID). Populated by ETL from Sprint + Issue join.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#branchName -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;branchName">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">branch name</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Git branch on which this commit was made. Literature-grounded: Git SCM branching model. Forward-compatible: pending Git integration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#buildSystem -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;buildSystem">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">build system</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The CI/CD system that generated this build failure e.g. Jenkins, Travis CI, GitHub Actions. Literature-grounded.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BuildFailure"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#canonicalLabel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;canonicalLabel">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">canonical label</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The normalised, canonical form of this term variant. ETL: derived from Issue.Title by lowercasing, removing punctuation, and stemming. Used as the primary matching key for synonym detection across projects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#carriedOver -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;carriedOver">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">carried over</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Whether this BacklogItem was not completed and carried to the next sprint. TAWOS stores only one Sprint_ID per issue (Issue.Sprint_ID, the current or last sprint), so this flag cannot be derived from the Issue table alone. It must be derived from sprint-assignment history, which TAWOS records in change_log rows where Field = &apos;Sprint&apos; (174,915 rows, Oct 2026 audit). True = the issue appears in more than one sprint assignment there.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#changedFiles -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;changedFiles">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">changed files</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Number of files modified in this commit. Literature-grounded: Git commit metadata. Forward-compatible property — large values signal high-risk commits for defect traceability. Pending Git integration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#clusterConfidence -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;clusterConfidence">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cluster confidence</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Confidence score for this synonym cluster. Range 0.0–1.0. Computed by ETL from term co-occurrence frequency across projects. Higher values indicate more reliable synonymy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SynonymCluster"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#clusterLabel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;clusterLabel">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cluster label</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The canonical concept label this SynonymCluster represents e.g. &apos;authentication&apos;, &apos;login&apos;, &apos;user-story&apos;. Used as the cluster&apos;s identifier for CQ8 resolution queries.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SynonymCluster"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#clusterSize -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;clusterSize">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cluster size</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Number of TermVariant individuals in this SynonymCluster. Minimum 2 — a cluster with one term is not a synonym cluster. Larger clusters indicate higher terminological diversity across TAWOS projects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SynonymCluster"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#commitDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;commitDate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">commit date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Timestamp of when this commit was pushed to the repository. Literature-grounded. Enables temporal RT chain analysis — commits after story closure indicate scope creep.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#commitHash -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;commitHash">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">commit hash</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The unique SHA hash identifying this commit in the Git repository. Literature-grounded: Git SCM. Primary key for CodeCommit individuals in future Git-integrated datasets.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#commitMessage -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;commitMessage">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">commit message</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The developer-authored message describing changes in this commit. Literature-grounded. Key field for NLP-based traceability recovery in planned BERT hybrid extension.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#completeDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;completeDate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">complete date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.Complete_Date (DateTime). When the sprint was formally closed. Only populated for CLOSED sprints. Key property for velocity and throughput analysis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#completionRate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;completionRate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">completion rate</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Percentage of sprint issues reaching Done/Closed status. Computed by ETL: throughput / totalIssues * 100. Query 17 confirms near-100% completion rate for most CLOSED TAWOS sprints. Key sprint health indicator.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#componentId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;componentId">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">component ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Component.ID (Int). Foreign key from issue_component table. Preserved for provenance and cross-project component matching in M4.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#componentName -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;componentName">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">component name</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Component.Name via issue_component junction table. The project component this artefact belongs to e.g. iOS, Android, Sharding, Administration. Represents project architecture decomposition — modelled as data property not class since components have no RT link participation in TAWOS Issue_Links. Top components: iOS (7,815) · Android (7,145) · Sharding (7,135) · Replication (6,712).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#confidenceScore -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;confidenceScore">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">confidence score</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Confidence of this TraceLink. Range: 0.0–1.0. AssertedLinks: 1.0 (ground truth). InferredLinks: set by SWRL rule confidence. Literature-grounded: supports future probabilistic RT extensions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#createdAt -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;createdAt">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">created at</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Creation_Date (DateTime). When this artefact was created.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#creatorId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;creatorId">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">creator ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Creator_ID (Int). Foreign key to User table. Who created this artefact in Jira.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#defectsFound -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;defectsFound">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">defects found</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Number of defects discovered during this test execution. Literature-grounded. When &gt; 0, connects TestResult to Bug individuals via isCausedBy property chain.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestResult"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#description -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;description">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">description</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Description_Text (Text). Free-text description.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#designLevel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;designLevel">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">design level</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The abstraction level of this design artefact. Values: System, Subsystem, Component, Module. Literature-grounded: IEEE 42010 Architecture Description standard.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#designVersion -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;designVersion">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">design version</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Version number of this design document e.g. v1.0, v2.3. Literature-grounded. Supports design evolution traceability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#documentType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;documentType">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">document type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The type of documentation artefact e.g. API documentation, user guide, release notes, inline comment. Literature-grounded.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Documentation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#documentUrl -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;documentUrl">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">document URL</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.URL (String). Link to the documentation resource. Optional — not all documentation issues have an external URL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Documentation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;anyURI"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#driftAuthorId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;driftAuthorId">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">drift author ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Change_Log.Author_ID (Int). Who made the terminological change. Foreign key to User table.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#driftDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;driftDate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">drift date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Change_Log.Creation_Date (DateTime). When this terminological change occurred. Enables temporal drift analysis — which sprint did the terminology change in?</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#driftEventId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;driftEventId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">drift event ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Change_Log.ID (Int). Primary key of the Change_Log row that triggered this DriftEvent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#driftIssueId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;driftIssueId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">drift issue ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Change_Log.Issue_ID (Int). The Issue whose title changed. Foreign key to Issue table — links DriftEvent back to the affected AgileArtefact.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#driftType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;driftType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">drift type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Classification of this drift event. Values: TitleDrift (Field=summary change) · LinkNameDrift (Issue_Links.Name does not map to TraceLinkType cluster) · StatusDrift (Field=status change affecting traceability). Primary source: TitleDrift from Change_Log. Secondary: LinkNameDrift from ETL mismatch detection.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#endDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;endDate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">end date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.End_Date (DateTime). Planned sprint end date. May differ from Complete_Date for overrun sprints.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#estimationDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;estimationDate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">estimation date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Estimation_Date (DateTime). When story points were estimated for this task.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#executionDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;executionDate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">execution date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">When this test was executed. Literature-grounded: IEEE 829. Supports temporal traceability analysis across sprints.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestResult"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#failedStage -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;failedStage">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">failed stage</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The pipeline stage at which the build failed e.g. compile, test, package, deploy. Literature-grounded. Connects to TestCase via verifies property when failure is test-related.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BuildFailure"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#fromLabel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;fromLabel">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">from label</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Change_Log.From_String (Text). The original title before the drift occurred. Preserved as the pre-drift term variant.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#hasEventStatus -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;hasEventStatus">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has event status</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Event ODP property. The current state of this Event e.g. Planned, Active, Completed. Mapped to Sprint.State in TAWOS in Step 5.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Event"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#inProgressMinutes -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;inProgressMinutes">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in progress (minutes)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.In_Progress_Minutes (Double). Total time the bug spent In Progress.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isAccepted -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;isAccepted">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is accepted</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Tracks whether this RequirementCandidate has been accepted into a sprint. Set to true by ETL when Issue.Sprint_ID IS NOT NULL AND Issue.Status = Done. NOTE: an earlier design (through v3) planned a SWRL rule to reclassify the individual to UserStory in place; this was abandoned because RequirementCandidate and UserStory are owl:disjointWith each other, which a live reclassification would violate under OWL-DL (HermiT would report the ontology inconsistent), and because SWRL is monotonic and cannot retract the original type regardless. isAccepted = true instead triggers an ETL step that mints a new UserStory individual and links it back to this one via arto:supersedes (see arto-m1-step3.ttl), preserving the acceptance decision trail without reclassification.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementCandidate"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isArchived -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;isArchived">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is archived</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Version.Archived (Boolean). True = this version is no longer actively maintained. Directly maps from TAWOS Version table boolean field.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isCompleted -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;isCompleted">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is completed</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Whether this BacklogItem was completed within its sprint. TAWOS: Issue.Status IN (&apos;Done&apos;,&apos;Closed&apos;). True = completed · False = carried over or incomplete. Core metric for sprint completion rate and velocity calculation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;BacklogItem"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isInferred -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;isInferred">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is inferred</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Whether this TraceLink was inferred by HermiT SWRL rules (true) or asserted directly from TAWOS Issue_Links (false). Core CQ6 property — enables inferred vs asserted link ratio calculation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#isReleased -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;isReleased">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is released</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Version.Released (Boolean). True = this version has been shipped to users. Directly maps from TAWOS Version table boolean field.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#issueId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;issueId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">issue ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.ID (Int). Primary key. Uniquely identifies any AgileArtefact individual.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#issueKey -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;issueKey">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">issue key</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Issue_Key (String). Human-readable Jira key e.g. PROJ-42.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#issueType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;issueType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">issue type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Type (String). Raw TAWOS type string preserved for provenance and M4 drift analysis. ETL routing uses this value to classify individuals into leaf classes.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#jiraSprintId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;jiraSprintId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Jira sprint ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.Jira_ID (Int). The Jira-internal sprint identifier. Preserved for cross-project sprint matching in M4.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#jiraVersionId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;jiraVersionId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Jira version ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Version.Jira_ID (Int). The Jira-internal version identifier. Preserved for provenance and cross-project version matching in M4.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#lastUpdated -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;lastUpdated">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">last updated</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Last_Updated (DateTime). Most recent modification timestamp.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#linkCreatedAt -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;linkCreatedAt">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">link created at</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: derived from Issue_Links creation context. When this trace link was established. Supports temporal RT chain analysis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#linkDirection -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;linkDirection">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">link direction</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue_Links.Direction (String). The Jira-level direction of this link e.g. inward, outward. Distinct from sdlcLinkDirection which captures SDLC phase direction.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#linkId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;linkId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">link ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue_Links.ID (Int). Primary key of the Issue_Links table. Uniquely identifies an AssertedLink individual.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#linkName -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;linkName">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">link name</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue_Links.Name (String). The raw TAWOS link type name e.g. Relates, Blocks, Duplicate. Preserved for M4 drift analysis and CQ7 distribution queries.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#maintenanceType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;maintenanceType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">maintenance type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Type (String). The raw TAWOS maintenance type — Documentation · Support Request · Build Failure · Problem Ticket. Preserved via arto:issueType but typed here for MaintenanceArtefact-specific querying.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#modellingTool -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;modellingTool">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">modelling tool</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The tool or notation used to produce this design artefact e.g. UML, ArchiMate, C4, ERD. Literature-grounded.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#passed -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;passed">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">passed</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Whether this test result passed or failed. Literature-grounded: IEEE 829. True = passed, False = failed. Key property for CQ3 test coverage analysis — failed TestResult individuals trigger defect traceability chain.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestResult"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#plannedVelocity -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;plannedVelocity">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">planned velocity</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Total story points committed at sprint planning. TAWOS: SUM(Issue.Story_Point WHERE Sprint_ID = s.ID AND Story_Point IS NOT NULL). Distinct from arto:velocity which counts only completed items.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintBacklog"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#priority -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;priority">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">priority</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Priority (String). Values: Highest, High, Medium, Low, Lowest.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#projectId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;projectId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">project ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Project_ID (Int). Foreign key to Project table. Identifies which of the 11 TAWOS projects this artefact belongs to.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#projectSource -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;projectSource">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">project source</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Project_ID (Int). Which of the 39 TAWOS projects this TermVariant originates from. Enables cross-project synonym detection — same canonical label appearing in multiple projects signals a synonym cluster.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#pullRequestUrl -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;pullRequestUrl">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pull request URL</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS bridge property: Issue.Pull_Request_URL (String). The one TAWOS field connecting issues to code-level artefacts. Present on 646 TAWOS issues (Story:347, Bug:154, Improvement:76, Technical task:27, New Feature:24, Task:18). Declared on ImplementationArtefact so all sprint-assigned artefacts can carry it.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;anyURI"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#rawLabel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;rawLabel">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">raw label</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Title (String). The original, unmodified title string as it appears in TAWOS. Preserved for provenance and M4 drift analysis. Multiple raw labels may share the same canonical label.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#releaseDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;releaseDate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">release date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Version.Release_Date (DateTime). When this version was released. NULL for unshipped versions. Key property for temporal RT chain analysis — commits after releaseDate indicate post-release defects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#reporterId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;reporterId">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reporter ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Reporter_ID (Int). Foreign key to User table. Who reported this artefact — relevant for Bug and SupportRequest traceability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#repositoryUrl -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;repositoryUrl">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">repository URL</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">URL of the Git repository containing this commit. Partially grounded: TAWOS Repository table contains 12 project repository URLs (Query 7). Full population pending Git API integration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;CodeCommit"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;anyURI"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#requirementSource -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;requirementSource">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">requirement source</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Reporter_ID (Int). Who raised this requirement — user, product owner, or stakeholder.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#resolution -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;resolution">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">resolution</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Resolution (String). How the bug was resolved e.g. Fixed, Won&apos;t Fix, Duplicate.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#resolutionDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;resolutionDate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">resolution date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Resolution_Date (DateTime). When this story was completed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#resolutionStatus -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;resolutionStatus">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">resolution status</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Resolution (String). How this maintenance artefact was resolved. Values vary by type: Documentation → Published/Outdated; SupportRequest → Resolved/Won&apos;t Fix; BuildFailure → Fixed/Known Issue.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#resolutionTimeMinutes -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;resolutionTimeMinutes">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">resolution time (minutes)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Resolution_Time_Minute (Double). Time taken to resolve the bug.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#resolvedByWordNet -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;resolvedByWordNet">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">resolved by WordNet</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Whether this synonym cluster was validated against WordNet synonym sets. True = WordNet confirms synonymy · False = TAWOS co-occurrence only. WordNet + Agile glossaries were planned as S4 conversion sources in Parts 3–4.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SynonymCluster"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sdlcLinkDirection -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sdlcLinkDirection">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SDLC link direction</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Direction of this TraceLink relative to the SDLC lifecycle. Set by ETL using source/target artefact class membership lookup. Values: Forward (Requirements→Implementation), Backward (Maintenance→Requirements), CrossCutting (Testing→Requirements), Horizontal (same SDLC phase). Enables CQ-SDLC1 full lifecycle chain queries.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sourcePhase -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sourcePhase">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">source phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SDLC phase of the source artefact. Set by ETL. Values: Requirements · Design · Implementation · Testing · Deployment · Maintenance. Used with targetPhase to determine sdlcLinkDirection.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sprintGoal -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sprintGoal">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sprint goal</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The stated objective of this sprint. TAWOS: partially available from Sprint.Name field — sprint names like &apos;BACKEND Sprint 17&apos; or &apos;Ingalls GA&apos; encode implicit goals. Full sprint goal text not stored in TAWOS — populated from Sprint.Name ETL parsing or left NULL for unnamed sprints. Literature-grounded: Scrum Guide sprint goal concept.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sprintId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sprintId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sprint ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.ID (Int). Primary key. Uniquely identifies a Sprint individual.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sprintName -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sprintName">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sprint name</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.Name (String). Human-readable sprint name e.g. &apos;Sprint 12&apos;, &apos;GDPR Followup Sprint 1&apos;. Names vary widely across projects — ETL preserves raw value for M4 drift analysis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sprintProjectId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sprintProjectId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sprint project ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.Project_ID (Int). Foreign key to Project table. Links sprint to one of the 39 TAWOS projects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#sprintState -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;sprintState">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sprint state</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.State (String). Confirmed values from Query 14: CLOSED · ACTIVE · FUTURE. ETL filter: WHERE Start_Date IS NOT NULL excludes virtual sprints (Kanban boards, version-named backlogs).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#startDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;startDate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">start date</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Sprint.Start_Date (DateTime). Sprint start. Together with endDate, realises the Time Indexed Situation pattern&apos;s time interval as plain data properties rather than a separate TimeInterval class. ETL filter: WHERE Start_Date IS NOT NULL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;dateTime"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#status -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;status">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">status</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Status (String). Workflow state e.g. To Do, In Progress, Done, Closed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#storyPointChangedAfterEstimation -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;storyPointChangedAfterEstimation">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">story point changed after estimation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Story_Point_Changed_After_Estimation (Boolean). Flags scope creep on this task.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;boolean"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#storyPoints -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;storyPoints">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">story points</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Story_Point (Double). Effort estimate. Only populated once a story is sprint-assigned.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#supportChannel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;supportChannel">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">support channel</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The channel through which this support request was received e.g. email, forum, helpdesk, community. Literature-grounded.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SupportRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#targetPhase -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;targetPhase">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">target phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SDLC phase of the target artefact. Set by ETL. Values: Requirements · Design · Implementation · Testing · Deployment · Maintenance.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#termFrequency -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;termFrequency">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">term frequency</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">How many times this term label appears in TAWOS across all issues. ETL: COUNT(Issue WHERE Title LIKE canonicalLabel). Higher frequency terms are more reliable synonym anchors.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#termType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;termType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">term type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ARTO class this TermVariant is associated with. Values: UserStory · Bug · Improvement · Suggestion · SprintTask · Documentation. Scopes synonym resolution to artefacts of the same type.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TermVariant"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#testEnvironment -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;testEnvironment">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">test environment</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The environment in which this test case is executed e.g. staging, production, CI. Literature-grounded.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestCase"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#testScript -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;testScript">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">test script</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The test script or procedure associated with this TestCase. Literature-grounded: IEEE 829 standard for software test documentation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestCase"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#testType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;testType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">test type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Type (String). Values: Test · Test Task. Preserved via arto:issueType but typed here for TestCase-specific querying.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestCase"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#testedBy -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;testedBy">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tested by</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The tester or automated system that executed this test. Literature-grounded: Maro et al. (2022) TracIMo. Connects to Developer/Agent in M3.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;TestResult"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#throughput -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;throughput">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">throughput</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Count of issues reaching Done or Closed status in this sprint. TAWOS: COUNT(Issue WHERE Sprint_ID = s.ID AND Status IN (&apos;Done&apos;,&apos;Closed&apos;)). Query 17 confirmed throughput ≈ total_issues for most CLOSED sprints — high completion rate across TAWOS projects. Complements velocity for teams not using story points.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#timeSpent -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;timeSpent">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">time spent</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Timespent (Double). Actual effort logged.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#title -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;title">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">title</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Title (String). Display name of the artefact.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#toLabel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;toLabel">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">to label</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Change_Log.To_String (Text). The new title after the drift occurred. The post-drift term variant.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;DriftEvent"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#totalEffortMinutes -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;totalEffortMinutes">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">total effort (minutes)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Issue.Total_Effort_Minutes (Double). Total effort logged against this task.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#totalIssues -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;totalIssues">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">total issues</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Total number of issues assigned to this sprint. TAWOS: COUNT(Issue WHERE Sprint_ID = s.ID). Query 17: range 5–87 issues per sprint across top 15 closed sprints. Denominator for sprint completion rate calculation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#velocity -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;velocity">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">velocity</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Sum of Story_Point values for all CLOSED/Done issues in this sprint. TAWOS: SUM(Issue.Story_Point WHERE Sprint_ID = s.ID AND Status IN (&apos;Done&apos;,&apos;Closed&apos;)). ETL outlier filter: WHERE Story_Point &lt; 1000 (Query 17 confirmed data quality issue: Ingalls GA = 26,710,115 story points). Standard Scrum velocity metric. Enables sprint-over-sprint velocity trend analysis for CQ7.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;decimal"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#versionId -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;versionId">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">version ID</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Version.ID (Int). Primary key of the Version table. Used as owl:hasKey for Version individuals.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;integer"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#versionName -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;versionName">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">version name</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TAWOS: Version.Name (String). Human-readable version identifier e.g. &apos;1.3 GA&apos;, &apos;2.0 M1&apos;, &apos;1.3 RC1&apos;. Raw string preserved — ETL parses this to set versionType.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#versionType -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="&arto;versionType">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&owl;FunctionalProperty"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">version type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Classification of this version derived from Version.Name by ETL. Values: Milestone (Name contains M1/M2/M3) · ReleaseCandidate (Name contains RC) · GeneralAvailability (Name contains GA or Released=1) · Planned (Release_Date IS NULL) · Other. Single flat class design — lifecycle distinction handled here rather than via subclasses due to inconsistent naming across 37 TAWOS projects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="&xsd;string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Classes
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#AgileArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;AgileArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Agile Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;issueKey"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;projectId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;title"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;issueType"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;issueId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;status"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Sprint"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Root superclass for all ARTO artefact classes. Scopes shared TAWOS Issue-table data properties. Generalises across all six SDLC phases via abstract intermediate classes introduced in Steps 1–5.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">S3 REUSE INTENT (not executed) — NeOn scenario S3, reuse of ontological resources:
arto:AgileArtefact was designed with Lapeña et al. (2019) in view — Improving
Traceability Links Recovery in Process Models through an Ontological Expansion of
Requirements. Advanced Information Systems Engineering (CAiSE 2019), LNCS 11483.
DOI: 10.1007/978-3-030-21290-2_17.

CORRECTION (Oct 2026): an earlier version of this annotation cited this paper
under a different title, venue and DOI (An Ontology for Software Traceability,
Requirements Engineering journal), described an Artefact class in it, and
recorded an intended bridge axiom arto:AgileArtefact rdfs:subClassOf
lapena:Artefact. None of that matches the CAiSE 2019 paper cited in this thesis.
Its ontology is a domain vocabulary of 27 concepts and 176 relationships
describing railway engineering terms, supplied by the authors&apos; industrial
partner and used to expand requirement text before Latent Semantic Indexing. It
defines no artefact class, so no bridge axiom was possible, and none is declared.

The paper does not state that this ontology is published (LORE&apos;s implementation
code is open source) — a known practical barrier to ontology reuse documented by
Martínez-García et al. (2022) as one of the top three impediments to S3 reuse in
academic ontology projects.

The intellectual alignment is preserved here via this rdfs:comment annotation
only. ARTO&apos;s AgileArtefact class is not aligned with any class in that ontology;
what the two works share is a concern with vocabulary mismatch between
requirement text and the artefacts it is traced to, which ARTO addresses
structurally through M4&apos;s synonym clusters.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;issueId"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#ArchitectureDocument -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;ArchitectureDocument">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Architecture Document</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;approvedBy"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;modellingTool"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;DesignModel"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Prototype"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal description of the system architecture at system or component level. Literature-grounded: IEEE 42010. Zero TAWOS individuals. Excluded from TAWOS Part 9 evaluation. Examples: system architecture specification, component interaction diagram, deployment diagram.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#AssertedLink -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;AssertedLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Asserted Link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;InferredLink"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A TraceLink directly populated from TAWOS Issue_Links table by the Python ETL pipeline. isInferred = false · assertionMethod = ETL · confidenceScore = 1.0. Corresponds to ground-truth RT links in the TAWOS dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BacklogItem -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;BacklogItem">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Backlog Item</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;carriedOver"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;isCompleted"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AgileArtefact as it appears within a SprintBacklog, carrying sprint-specific context: priority order, completion status, and carryover flag. TAWOS: Issue WHERE Sprint_ID IS NOT NULL (7,967 sprint-assigned issues). BacklogItem is a context-dependent view of an AgileArtefact within a specific sprint — the same AgileArtefact can appear as a BacklogItem in multiple sprints if carried over. Linked to its source AgileArtefact via arto:refersToArtefact property.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BackwardSDLCLink -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;BackwardSDLCLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Backward SDLC Link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A TraceLink where the source artefact belongs to a later SDLC phase than the target — defect traceability upstream. sdlcLinkDirection = Backward. Examples: Bug reportedIn UserStory (Maintenance→Requirements), BuildFailure relatesTo CodeCommit (Maintenance→Implementation). Critical for CQ4 impact propagation analysis. Set by ETL.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Bug -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Bug">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bug</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;DefectArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;resolution"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;inProgressMinutes"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;resolutionTimeMinutes"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A defect discovered during or after implementation. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Bug (215,570) — dominant artefact type, nearly 7x larger than Story. Participates actively in RT chain via causes, reportedIn, and relatesTo properties. Migrates under MaintenanceArtefact in Step 5.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BuildFailure -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;BuildFailure">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Build Failure</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;failedStage"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;buildSystem"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;DefectArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Documentation"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;ProblemTicket"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;SupportRequest"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A CI/CD pipeline build failure tracked as a Jira issue. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Build Failure (1,715 individuals). RT links: 81 confirmed in Query 13 (Duplicate with itself and Task). Zero sprint-assigned — purely a maintenance/operations artefact. Connects to Bug via isCausedBy when build failure introduces a defect.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#CodeCommit -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;CodeCommit">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Code Commit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;authorId"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;commitMessage"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;repositoryUrl"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;commitDate"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;commitHash"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;changedFiles"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;branchName"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;SprintTask"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A unit of source code change pushed to a version control repository, implementing one or more SprintTasks. Literature-grounded: Git SCM and Agile framework glossaries; conceptually echoes the Satisfaction category of Ramesh and Jarke (2001) without claiming a specific named sub-type. No TAWOS individuals — TAWOS Repository table stores Jira instance URLs not Git repositories (Query 7). TAWOS Pull_Request_URL (646 issues) bridges to code level via arto:pullRequestUrl. Excluded from Part 9 evaluation — documented as dataset limitation L3. Forward-compatible: full population pending Git API integration or future dataset with commit-level data.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#CrossCuttingLink -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;CrossCuttingLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cross Cutting Link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A TraceLink that spans non-adjacent SDLC phases skipping intermediate phases. sdlcLinkDirection = CrossCutting. Examples: TestCase verifies UserStory (Testing→Requirements skipping Design and Implementation), Version containedIn UserStory (Deployment→Requirements). Represents high-level governance links in the RT chain. Set by ETL.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DefectArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;DefectArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Defect Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;DeploymentArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Documentation"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;ProblemTicket"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;SupportRequest"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract defect phase class. Declared here as a named class — rdfs:subClassOf declared in Step 5 where DefectArtefact migrates under MaintenanceArtefact. Generalisation point for non-TAWOS datasets — Defect, Fault, Error subclass here. Leaf classes in Step 1: Bug.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">MIGRATED in Step 5: DefectArtefact now SubClassOf MaintenanceArtefact (was SubClassOf AgileArtefact in Step 1). Defect management is a maintenance-phase activity. Single rdfs:subClassOf re-declaration — no property or individual rework required. Bug inherits new parent automatically.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DeploymentArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;DeploymentArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Deployment Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract SDLC Deployment phase class. Groups Version and PlannedRelease. TAWOS grounding: Version table (5,639 records across 37 projects) + Issue.Type = Release (4) + Milestone (44). Strongly grounded — Fix_Version junction table holds 224,254 total rows and Affected_Version holds 264,004 total rows (verified via direct COUNT, Oct 2026 audit), linking Bug, Improvement, Task, Story, and New Feature individuals to Version instances.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DesignArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;DesignArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Design Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;designVersion"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;designLevel"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract SDLC Design phase class. Groups ArchitectureDocument, DesignModel, and Prototype. Zero TAWOS individuals — no design-specific Issue.Type exists in TAWOS (confirmed Query 12). Introduced for multi-dataset comparability (addresses limitation L3) — any dataset with design artefacts maps here without ontology modification. Excluded from TAWOS Part 9 evaluation scope. Generalisation point for non-TAWOS datasets using hybrid Agile-waterfall methodologies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DesignModel -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;DesignModel">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Design Model</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;modellingTool"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Prototype"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal or semi-formal model representing system structure or behaviour. Literature-grounded: UML 2.5, C4 model, ArchiMate 3.1. Zero TAWOS individuals. Excluded from TAWOS Part 9 evaluation. Examples: class diagram, sequence diagram, data model, API specification, entity-relationship diagram.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Documentation -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Documentation">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Documentation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;documentUrl"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;documentType"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;ProblemTicket"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;SupportRequest"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A documentation artefact tracking the creation or update of technical or user documentation. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Documentation (699 individuals). RT links confirmed: 5 links (verified via direct OUTBOUND-only COUNT against the live TAWOS database, Oct 2026 audit; supersedes an earlier estimate of 114 that double-counted both link directions) in Reference/Duplicate/Relates with Bug/Story/Improvement. New RT property: documents (Documentation → AgileArtefact).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DriftEvent -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;DriftEvent">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Drift Event</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;driftEventId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;affectsArtefact"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;fromLabel"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;driftDate"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;driftType"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;toLabel"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A detected terminological change in TAWOS artefact labels. Primary source: Change_Log WHERE Field = &apos;summary&apos; — title changes captured via From_String (old label) and To_String (new label) with Creation_Date timestamp. Secondary source: Issue_Links.Name values not mapping to any M2 TraceLinkType cluster (LinkNameDrift). Full Change_Log integration deferred: MySQL full scan timeouts at 30s — future ETL requires CREATE INDEX ON Change_Log(Field). Lightweight ETL: sample 1,000 summary changes per project using LIMIT clause.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;driftEventId"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Epic -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Epic">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Epic</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementCandidate"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A large body of work decomposed into UserStories or RequirementCandidates. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Epic (4,157). Sits at the top of the requirements decomposition chain: Epic → UserStory → SprintTask.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Event -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Event">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Event</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract Time Indexed Situation ODP anchor class (S7). Source: http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl. Instantiated by arto:Sprint in Step 5 — a Sprint is a time-bounded Event with a defined start date, end date, and status. Introduced here as an anchor for the Event ODP before the full M3 Sprint module is built.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#ForwardSDLCLink -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;ForwardSDLCLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Forward SDLC Link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A TraceLink where the source artefact belongs to an earlier SDLC phase than the target. sdlcLinkDirection = Forward. Examples: UserStory hasImplementingTask SprintTask (Requirements→Implementation), SprintTask tracesTo CodeCommit (Implementation→Implementation), TestCase verifies UserStory (Testing→Requirements is CrossCutting not Forward). Set by ETL.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#ImplementationArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;ImplementationArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Implementation Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract SDLC Implementation phase class. Groups all implementation-level artefacts. Completed in Step 3 with CodeCommit. Generalisation point for non-TAWOS datasets — PullRequest, Branch, ChangeSet subclass here. Leaf classes in Step 1: SprintTask.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Improvement -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Improvement">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Improvement</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementCandidate"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;NewFeature"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Suggestion"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A proposed enhancement to existing functionality, not yet sprint-accepted. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Improvement (42,691).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#InferredLink -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;InferredLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Inferred Link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLink"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A TraceLink discovered by HermiT via SWRL rules — not present in TAWOS Issue_Links. isInferred = true · assertionMethod = SWRL · confidenceScore set per rule. Represents latent traceability recovered by ARTO&apos;s reasoning layer. Core CQ6 contribution — quantifies ARTO&apos;s inferential power over raw TAWOS data.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#MaintenanceArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Maintenance Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;maintenanceType"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract SDLC Maintenance phase class. Groups DefectArtefact (migrated from AgileArtefact), Documentation, SupportRequest, BuildFailure, and ProblemTicket. TAWOS grounding: Documentation (699) · SupportRequest (2,368) · BuildFailure (1,715) · ProblemTicket (113) · Bug (215,570 via DefectArtefact). TechnicalDebt (30 individuals, zero RT links) ETL-filtered — mapped to arto:Improvement via skos:closeMatch in M4. Change_Log table (Query 15) provides M4 drift sources: summary (83,599) · description (264,504) · Link (448,089) change records.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#NewFeature -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;NewFeature">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">New Feature</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementCandidate"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Suggestion"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A net-new capability request not yet sprint-accepted. TAWOS: Issue.Type = New Feature (14,239).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#OrphanArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;OrphanArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Orphan Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:complementOf>
                            <owl:Restriction>
                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
                                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&owl;Thing"/>
                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:complementOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:complementOf>
                            <owl:Restriction>
                                <owl:onProperty>
                                    <rdf:Description>
                                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="&arto;hasTraceLink"/>
                                    </rdf:Description>
                                </owl:onProperty>
                                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&owl;Thing"/>
                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:complementOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Formal definition of an orphan artefact: an AgileArtefact with no outgoing and no incoming hasTraceLink. This matches the direction-inclusive CQ5 query. An individual can be simultaneously a UserStory AND an OrphanArtefact. Under the open world assumption HermiT does not populate this class, because a missing link is unknown rather than absent. CQ5 orphan detection is therefore performed by a closed world SPARQL MINUS query (see R4 in arto-m2-traceability.ttl). Defined with complementOf + someValuesFrom rather than a cardinality restriction, because hasTraceLink is not simple in OWL 2 DL (v1.1.0).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#PlannedRelease -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;PlannedRelease">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Planned Release</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;DeploymentArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;Version"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A planned release event tracked as a Jira issue. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Release (4 individuals). Distinct from arto:Version — PlannedRelease is an Issue-level planning artefact while Version is a Version-table record. All 4 PlannedRelease individuals have Fix_Version populated (Query 11) — directly linked to Version instances via fixedIn property.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#ProblemTicket -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;ProblemTicket">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Problem Ticket</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;SupportRequest"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal problem record tracking a recurring or systemic issue. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Problem Ticket (113 individuals). RT links: 29 confirmed in Query 13 (Related/Duplicate with Bug). Semantically distinct from Bug — a ProblemTicket tracks a systemic pattern while Bug tracks a specific defect instance.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Prototype -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Prototype">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prototype</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;DesignArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A preliminary working model or mockup used to validate design decisions. Literature-grounded: Agile framework design practices, lean UX. Zero TAWOS individuals. Excluded from TAWOS Part 9 evaluation. Examples: UI wireframe, clickable mockup, proof-of-concept implementation, paper prototype.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#RequirementCandidate -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;RequirementCandidate">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Requirement Candidate</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;isAccepted"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;UserStory"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A proposed requirement not yet accepted into a sprint. Intermediate class grouping Suggestion, Improvement, and NewFeature. Addresses literature gap G2 (pre-acceptance traceability). When isAccepted = true, ETL mints a new UserStory individual linked back to this one via arto:supersedes (Step 3); the original individual keeps its RequirementCandidate typing permanently as an immutable acceptance record, since RequirementCandidate is owl:disjointWith UserStory.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#RequirementsArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;RequirementsArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Requirements Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;requirementSource"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract SDLC Requirements phase class. Groups all requirement-level artefacts. Generalisation point for non-TAWOS datasets — external requirement types subclass here rather than at leaf level. Leaf classes in Step 1: Epic, UserStory, RequirementCandidate and its subclasses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Sprint -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Sprint">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sprint</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;Event"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;sprintProjectId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;sprintName"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;sprintState"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;sprintId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A time-bounded Agile iteration containing a set of UserStories and SprintTasks. Instantiates Time Indexed Situation ODP (S7) — Sprint SubClassOf arto:Event. TAWOS: Sprint table with Start_Date, End_Date, State, Project_ID. Full Sprint module with all properties, belongsToSprint, and M3 bridge axioms built in Step 5.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl"/>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;sprintId"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#SprintBacklog -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;SprintBacklog">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sprint Backlog</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;backlogId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ordered set of BacklogItems committed to a Sprint at sprint planning. TAWOS: set of Issue records WHERE Sprint_ID IS NOT NULL, grouped by Sprint_ID. One SprintBacklog per Sprint — declared Functional on hasBacklog property. Contains UserStory, SprintTask, Bug and other AgileArtefact individuals assigned to the sprint. Bridges Sprint (M3) to AgileArtefact individuals (M1) via hasBacklogItem property.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;backlogId"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#SprintTask -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;SprintTask">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sprint Task</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;ImplementationArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;belongsToSprint"/>
                <owl:maxCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:maxCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;estimationDate"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;storyPointChangedAfterEstimation"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;totalEffortMinutes"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A unit of implementation work assigned to a sprint, decomposed from a UserStory. TAWOS: Issue.Type IN (Task, Sub-task, Technical task) WHERE Sprint_ID IS NOT NULL (7,967 total). Raw type preserved in arto:issueType for provenance and M4 drift analysis. Sprint-unassigned instances filtered by ETL until Step 5.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Suggestion -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Suggestion">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Suggestion</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementCandidate"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A user-submitted idea not yet formally accepted as a requirement. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Suggestion (96,370). Largest RequirementCandidate subtype in TAWOS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#SupportRequest -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;SupportRequest">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Support Request</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;MaintenanceArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;supportChannel"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;affectedUsers"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A user-reported support or help request. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Support Request (2,368 individuals — highest maintenance volume). RT links: 154 confirmed in Query 13 (Reference/Duplicate/Cause with Suggestion/Bug). Only 4 sprint-assigned — primarily a post-release maintenance artefact.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#SynonymCluster -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;SynonymCluster">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Synonym Cluster</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;clusterSize"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;hasVariant"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">2</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;clusterLabel"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A group of TermVariant individuals that represent the same concept across different TAWOS projects or within the same project over time. Minimum 2 TermVariants required. When SWRL Rule R3 fires on two artefacts linked via skos:exactMatch through their TermVariants, trace links propagate across the cluster. Implements the skos:ConceptScheme pattern for terminology management.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;clusterLabel"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TermVariant -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;TermVariant">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Term Variant</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;rawLabel"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;projectSource"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;refersToIssue"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;canonicalLabel"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A terminological variant of an artefact concept label across TAWOS projects. Two TermVariants representing the same concept in different projects are linked via skos:exactMatch, enabling SWRL Rule R3 to propagate trace links across project boundaries. TAWOS: derived from Issue.Title normalisation — lowercased, punctuation-removed, stemmed. Core M4 class contributing to literature gap G2 (narrow scope and rigid structure, Chapter 6): M4 reconciles terminology that differs across projects, so artefacts from different projects can be traced together.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;canonicalLabel"/>
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;projectSource"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TestCase -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;TestCase">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Test Case</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;testEnvironment"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;testScript"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;testType"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&arto;TestResult"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A specification of conditions under which a UserStory or SprintTask is verified. TAWOS: Issue.Type IN (Test, Test Task) WHERE Sprint_ID IS NOT NULL (353 total). Thin TAWOS population — Test (17) + Test Task (336). Included in Part 9 evaluation with expected low recall due to dataset sparsity. Distinct from TestResult: TestCase is the specification, TestResult is the execution outcome.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TestResult -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;TestResult">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Test Result</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;TestingArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;executionDate"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;defectsFound"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;passed"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The outcome of executing a TestCase against a UserStory or SprintTask. Literature-grounded: IEEE 829. No TAWOS individuals — TAWOS does not store test execution outcomes. Excluded from Part 9 precision/recall evaluation (zero TP/FP/FN). Forward-compatible infrastructure: pending test execution data integration. When passed = false, connects to Bug individuals via isCausedBy property chain.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TestingArtefact -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;TestingArtefact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Testing Artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;AgileArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract SDLC Testing phase class. Groups TestCase and TestResult. TAWOS grounding: Test (17) + Test Task (336) = 353 individuals. Generalisation point for non-TAWOS datasets — QATicket, TestSuite, TestPlan subclass here. Leaf classes: TestCase, TestResult.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TraceLink -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;TraceLink">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Trace Link</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;confidenceScore"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;hasLinkType"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;hasTargetArtefact"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;isInferred"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;assertionMethod"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;hasSourceArtefact"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A directed traceability link between two AgileArtefact individuals. Root class for AssertedLink, InferredLink, ForwardSDLCLink, BackwardSDLCLink, and CrossCuttingLink. Each TraceLink individual carries source/target artefacts, link type (semantic cluster), SDLC direction, and assertion method. Bridges M1 artefact hierarchy to M2 traceability analysis.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;linkId"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#TraceLinkType -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;TraceLinkType">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Trace Link Type</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Controlled vocabulary class for RT link semantic clusters. 7 named individuals cover all 24 ARTO RT properties grouped by semantic meaning. Each TraceLink individual points to exactly one TraceLinkType via arto:hasLinkType. Enables CQ7 link type distribution queries without enumerating all 24 individual property names.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#UserStory -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;UserStory">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">User Story</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;RequirementsArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;timeSpent"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;storyPoints"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;acceptanceCriteria"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;resolutionDate"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;belongsToSprint"/>
                <owl:maxCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:maxCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A committed, sprint-assigned requirement expressed from a user perspective. TAWOS: Issue.Type = Story (31,394). Central RT chain node — CQ1–CQ7 all reference UserStory directly or transitively. Deliberately kept owl:disjointWith RequirementCandidate — see arto:isAccepted for why. Accepted RequirementCandidates are represented as new UserStory individuals connected back via arto:supersedes, not by reclassifying the original individual.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Version -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&arto;Version">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Version</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&arto;DeploymentArtefact"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;isReleased"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;isArchived"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;versionName"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;versionType"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;versionId"/>
                <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&arto;releaseDate"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="&xsd;nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A named point in the software release lifecycle — milestone, release candidate, or general availability release. TAWOS: Version table (5,639 records). Single flat class with versionType data property (Milestone/ReleaseCandidate/GeneralAvailability/Planned/Other) — subclasses avoided due to inconsistent naming conventions across 37 TAWOS projects (Query 9a). Also absorbs Issue.Type = Milestone (44 individuals) via versionType = Milestone. Primary RT hub for deployment-level traceability: Fix_Version junction table holds 224,254 total rows; Affected_Version holds 264,004 total rows (verified via direct COUNT, Oct 2026 audit; both figures supersede an earlier, lower per-artefact-type breakdown that undercounted by summing distinct-Bug-with-a-version-entry rather than total junction rows).</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:hasKey rdf:parseType="Collection">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&arto;versionId"/>
        </owl:hasKey>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Individuals
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#ARTONetwork -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;ARTONetwork">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO Network Metadata</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO Network Structure (v1.2.0)

MODULES:
  M1 Artefact Module (5 steps — arto-m1-step1-v5 to step5):
    Classes: 30 (7 SDLC abstracts + 22 leaf classes + OrphanArtefact)
    RT Properties: 24 + 21 inverses + hasTraceLink superproperty
    ODP: Part-Whole (hasPart) · Event (Sprint) — conceptual level
    TAWOS grounding: Queries 1-12 (15 SQL queries total)
    Key decision: DefectArtefact migrated under MaintenanceArtefact
                  in Step 5; DesignArtefact for multi-dataset
                  comparability (zero TAWOS, excluded from Part 9)

  M2 Traceability Module (arto-m2-traceability):
    Classes: TraceLink + AssertedLink + InferredLink +
             ForwardSDLCLink + BackwardSDLCLink + CrossCuttingLink
    Controlled vocabulary: TraceLinkType + 7 named individuals
    Rules: R1 impact inference (CQ4) · R2 test coverage (CQ3/CQ5)
           encoded here as executable SWRL (R1a–R1e, R2a–R2b).
           R3 (CQ8) is encoded in M4. R4 (CQ5) is documentation only:
           orphan detection needs negation, which SWRL cannot express.
    Key property: impacts (Transitive + SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink)
    sdlcLinkDirection: set by ETL (Forward/Backward/CrossCutting/
                       Horizontal) via SDLC phase lookup table

  M3 Sprint Module (arto-m3-sprint):
    Classes: SprintBacklog · BacklogItem
    Metrics: velocity · throughput · completionRate · totalIssues
    Bridge chain: Sprint→hasBacklog→SprintBacklog→
                  hasBacklogItem→BacklogItem→refersToArtefact→
                  AgileArtefact
    Agent: assigneeId/creatorId/reporterId as data properties
           (AgentRole ODP dropped — User table has only ID)
    TAWOS: Queries 14, 16, 17 confirmed velocity/throughput

  M4 Semantic Resolution Module (arto-m4-semantic):
    Classes: TermVariant · SynonymCluster · DriftEvent
    SKOS: exactMatch and closeMatch declared as object properties
          (not imported; no symmetry or transitivity asserted)
          exactMatch: 4 class-level mappings (M4) + 2 pilot pairs
                      (story_001/story_equiv · bug_001/bug_equiv)
          closeMatch: 6 class-level mappings
    SWRL R3: R3a forward · R3b backward · R3c impacts propagation
             across exact synonyms (executable, encoded in M4)
    DriftEvent: lightweight from Change_Log WHERE Field=summary
                (full integration deferred — MySQL timeout)
    ETL synonym detection: Duplicate Issue_Links co-occurrence

BRIDGE AXIOMS (5 active):
  BA3: hasTraceLink domain/range AgileArtefact (M1→M2)
  BA4: UserStory belongsToSprint Sprint maxCard 1 (M1→M3)
  BA5: SprintTask belongsToSprint Sprint maxCard 1 (M1→M3)
  BA6: TermVariant refersToIssue AgileArtefact (M4→M1)
  BA7: impacts SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink (M2 SWRL→M1)

REUSE SUMMARY (NeOn scenario numbers corrected Oct 2026 to match
the canonical NeOn numbering; see Chapter 6, Section 6.4):
  S3 (reuse of ontological resources): INTENT not executed — Lapeña
     (2019) and Pakdeetrakulwong (2015) OWL files unavailable.
     Documented via rdfs:comment annotations. No fabricated IRIs
     declared.
  S2 (re-engineering from a non-ontological resource): TAWOS SQL
     queries → OWL-DL RT property hierarchy (24 properties, 7
     semantic clusters). Ramesh and Jarke&apos;s (2001) four top-level
     categories provided coarse-grained structuring influence only
     — the 24 properties were not derived from specific named
     sub-types in their taxonomy (see Chapter 6, Section 6.5).
  S7 (reuse of ontology design patterns): Part-Whole + Event ODPs
     at conceptual instantiation level. rdfs:isDefinedBy in module
     files.
     owl:imports of ODP files not used — avoids namespace
     conflicts without CQ benefit.
  S2 (conversion, continued): the TAWOS relational schema was converted
     to OWL via 15 SQL queries; Agile glossary synonyms → SKOS in M4.

COMPETENCY QUESTIONS:
  CQ1: story→task decomposition + sprint context
  CQ2: bug→story defect traceability
  CQ3: test coverage gaps (verifies + SPARQL MINUS)
  CQ4: impact propagation (SWRL R1 + impacts transitivity)
  CQ5: orphan artefact detection (OrphanArtefact + SPARQL MINUS)
  CQ6: inferred vs asserted link ratio (isInferred on TraceLink)
  CQ7: link type distribution (TraceLinkType 7 clusters)
  CQ8: synonym resolution (skos:exactMatch + SWRL R3)

TAWOS EVALUATION SCOPE (Part 9):
  INCLUDED: Epic · UserStory · Suggestion · Improvement ·
            NewFeature · SprintTask · Bug · TestCase ·
            Version · PlannedRelease · Documentation ·
            SupportRequest · BuildFailure · ProblemTicket ·
            SprintBacklog · BacklogItem · TermVariant ·
            SynonymCluster · DriftEvent
  EXCLUDED (zero TAWOS individuals, N/A in metrics):
            CodeCommit · TestResult · ArchitectureDocument ·
            DesignModel · Prototype
  EVALUATION: per-class precision/recall/F1 + macro/micro avg
  BASELINE: VSM + LSI keyword matching (same TAWOS projects)
  ABLATION: ARTO without SWRL rules (no R1–R3) as control</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#AssociativeLink_Type -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;AssociativeLink_Type">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume rdf:datatype="&xsd;integer">57779</arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Associative</arto:TraceLinkType_label>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_properties rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">relatesTo · references · supersedes</arto:TraceLinkType_properties>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">General associative RT links with no specific directional or structural meaning. All Issue_Links counts OUTBOUND-only (Oct 2026 audit; each link is stored once INBOUND and once OUTBOUND), mapped through arto_link_type_lookup. relatesTo 37,265 (Relates 22,739 + Related 12,754 + Detail 1,048 + Problem/Incident 380 + Relate 344) + references 19,914 (Reference) + supersedes 600 (Supersession 381 + Supercedes 180 + Supersede 39) = 57,779. Largest cluster by volume — backbone of the TAWOS RT network. Supersedes the earlier figure of 112,874, which double-counted both link directions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BA3_Bridge -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;BA3_Bridge">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BA3 — M1→M2 Bridge</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">BRIDGE AXIOM BA3: hasTraceLink domain and range declared on AgileArtefact — connects M1 artefact individuals to M2 traceability properties. All 24 RT properties are SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink. SWRL rules R1 and R2 (M2) and R3 (M4) fire on AgileArtefact individuals loaded from M1 module files.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BA4_Bridge -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;BA4_Bridge">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BA4 — M1→M3 UserStory-Sprint Bridge</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">BRIDGE AXIOM BA4: UserStory belongsToSprint Sprint (maxCardinality 1). Connects M1 RequirementsArtefact individuals to M3 Sprint individuals. Required for CQ1 sprint context queries. Each UserStory assigned to at most one Sprint per iteration — enforced as maxCardinality restriction at root level.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BA5_Bridge -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;BA5_Bridge">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BA5 — M1→M3 SprintTask-Backlog Bridge</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">BRIDGE AXIOM BA5: SprintTask individuals appear as BacklogItem individuals in SprintBacklogs via arto:refersToArtefact (M3). SprintTask also carries belongsToSprint (maxCardinality 1) at root level. Connects M1 ImplementationArtefact individuals to M3 sprint planning structure. Required for full chain query: Sprint→SprintBacklog→BacklogItem→SprintTask.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BA6_Bridge -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;BA6_Bridge">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BA6 — M4→M1 TermVariant-Artefact Bridge</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">BRIDGE AXIOM BA6: TermVariant refersToIssue AgileArtefact (Functional). Connects M4 semantic resolution individuals to M1 artefact individuals. Core M4-M1 bridge: when two TermVariants in the same SynonymCluster refer to artefacts in different projects, skos:exactMatch declared between those artefacts enables SWRL Rule R3 to propagate trace links across project boundaries. Required for CQ8.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BA7_Bridge -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;BA7_Bridge">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BA7 — M2 SWRL→M1 impacts Bridge</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">BRIDGE AXIOM BA7: impacts SubPropertyOf hasTraceLink. Ensures every impacts link, whether asserted, derived by SWRL R1, or extended by the transitivity of impacts, also counts as a hasTraceLink for the reasoner. Without this bridge, inferred impacts would not appear in hasTraceLink-based coverage. Note: Protégé&apos;s embedded SPARQL engine reads asserted triples only, so inferred links reach the CQ5 MINUS query only once they are materialised. Also makes hasTraceLink non-simple (impacts is transitive), which is why no cardinality restriction is placed on hasTraceLink. Critical for CQ4 (impact propagation) and CQ5 (orphan detection).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Bug -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;Bug">
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="&arto;Defect"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#BuildFailure -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;BuildFailure">
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="&arto;Bug"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Defect -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;Defect"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DefectLink_Type -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;DefectLink_Type">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume rdf:datatype="&xsd;integer">1596</arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Defect</arto:TraceLinkType_label>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_properties rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">causes · reportedIn · fixes · addresses</arto:TraceLinkType_properties>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defect traceability links connecting bugs to their origin and resolution artefacts. All Issue_Links counts OUTBOUND-only (Oct 2026 audit; each link is stored once INBOUND and once OUTBOUND), mapped through arto_link_type_lookup. causes 1,444 (Cause 1,250 + Caused 194) + fixes 130 (Fixes 98 + Resolve 32) + addresses 22 (Addresses) = 1,596 Issue_Links. Regression is no longer counted here: it was reassigned to verifies (M1 Step 3). reportedIn has no TAWOS source: TAWOS records no explicit reported-in link, and its Bug→Story links are mostly Relates, Blocks and Duplicate (M1 Step 2). It is used in the pilot only. The earlier figure of 2,425 counted every Bug–Story link in both directions. Critical for BackwardSDLCLink classification. Supersedes the earlier figure of 10,452.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DependencyLink_Type -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;DependencyLink_Type">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume rdf:datatype="&xsd;integer">18957</arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Dependency</arto:TraceLinkType_label>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_properties rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">dependsOn · blocks · hasImplementingTask · follows · impacts</arto:TraceLinkType_properties>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Prerequisite and ordering dependencies between artefacts. All Issue_Links counts OUTBOUND-only (Oct 2026 audit; each link is stored once INBOUND and once OUTBOUND), mapped through arto_link_type_lookup. dependsOn 9,763 (Depends 5,103 + Dependency 4,173 + dependent 266 + Depend 169 + Required 52) + blocks 9,169 (Blocks 4,211 + Blockers 3,124 + Blocker 1,428 + Block 396 + Blocked 10) + follows 25 (Follows) = 18,957 Issue_Links. follows (ordering without a hard dependency) was added in v1.1.0; it was previously in no cluster. impacts is also a member: it is inferred by SWRL R1 and the transitivity of impacts, never loaded from TAWOS, so it adds nothing to the volume (pilot link_005 already types an impacts link as DependencyLink_Type). hasStory (173) was moved to the Structural cluster in v1.1.0: an Epic containing UserStories is a part-whole relationship, as M1 Step 2 already records. hasImplementingTask (338 links: Story→Task/Sub-task links in the Associative and Structural clusters, OUTBOUND-only, Nov 2026, M1 Step 2) is asserted by issue type pair on top of the raw-name property, so those links are already counted above and are not added again here. Supersedes the earlier figure of 38,773, which double-counted both link directions and included hasStory.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DeploymentLink_Type -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;DeploymentLink_Type">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume rdf:datatype="&xsd;integer">488258</arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Deployment</arto:TraceLinkType_label>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_properties rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">fixedIn · affectedIn</arto:TraceLinkType_properties>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Deployment lifecycle links connecting artefacts to Version records. Sourced from the TAWOS fix_version and affected_version junction tables, not Issue_Links (Nov 2026 audit). fixedIn 224,254 rows (fix_version; largest: Bug 129,501 · Task 20,807 · Improvement 24,981 · Suggestion 16,722 · Sub-task 10,493 · Story 8,587 · New Feature 8,036) + affectedIn 264,004 rows (affected_version; largest: Bug 202,384 · Improvement 29,620 · New Feature 8,008 · Task 7,979 · Sub-task 7,394 · Story 2,289) = 488,258. Every row is a distinct (issue, version) pair and joins to an issue; junction tables have no direction, so there is no INBOUND/OUTBOUND double counting. Rows on issue types that ARTO does not load as classes (e.g. Question, Wish, Investigation, Technical Debt, Incident) are dropped by the ETL. Largest cluster by volume. Supersedes the earlier figure of 235,324, whose components (141,347 + 160,602) matched neither table.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DesignLink_Type -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;DesignLink_Type">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume rdf:datatype="&xsd;integer">6012</arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Design</arto:TraceLinkType_label>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_properties rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">refines · realizes · derives · tracesTo · verifies · documents</arto:TraceLinkType_properties>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Design and verification lifecycle links. TAWOS, all counts OUTBOUND-only (Oct 2026 audit; each link is stored once INBOUND and once OUTBOUND): verifies/Tested+QA Test+Bonfire Testing+Regression (5,426) + derives/Derived+Issue split+Split (570) + realizes/Implements (11) + documents/Documented (5) + tracesTo (literature) + refines (literature) = 6,012 TAWOS-grounded links plus literature-grounded properties for multi-dataset comparability. Supersedes earlier figures (7,416; then 7,191 and 7,172) that mixed double-counted and audited component counts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#DuplicationLink_Type -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;DuplicationLink_Type">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="&arto;TraceLinkType"/>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume rdf:datatype="&xsd;integer">29456</arto:TraceLinkType_tawosVolume>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Duplication</arto:TraceLinkType_label>
        <arto:TraceLinkType_properties rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">duplicates</arto:TraceLinkType_properties>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Duplicate artefact detection links. All Issue_Links counts OUTBOUND-only (Oct 2026 audit; each link is stored once INBOUND and once OUTBOUND), mapped through arto_link_type_lookup. duplicates 29,456 (Duplicate). Cloners (3,780) is deliberately excluded: clone provenance is administrative, not a traceability relationship. Second largest cluster by volume. Critical for M4 synonym resolution. Supersedes the earlier figure of 66,470, which double-counted both directions and included Cloners.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#EnhancementRequest -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;EnhancementRequest"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Improvement -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;Improvement">
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="&arto;EnhancementRequest"/>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="&arto;TechnicalDebt"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Investigation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;Investigation"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Iteration -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;Iteration"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#P1_RequirementCandidatePromotion -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;P1_RequirementCandidatePromotion">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P1 — RequirementCandidate Promotion (ETL pattern, not SWRL)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">P1 — RequirementCandidate Promotion (CQ-PROMO)

WHY THIS IS NOT A SWRL RULE:
The original methodology (M1 Step 1, through v3) planned this as a
SWRL rule: RequirementCandidate(?rc) ^ isAccepted(?rc, true) -&gt; UserStory(?rc).
This is unimplementable as written: RequirementCandidate and UserStory
are declared owl:disjointWith each other, so a reasoner firing this
rule would find the individual satisfying two disjoint classes and
report the whole ontology inconsistent — not merely that individual
unsatisfiable. SWRL&apos;s monotonicity compounds the problem: even if
disjointness were relaxed, the rule could only add the UserStory type,
never retract the original RequirementCandidate subtype, so the
individual would carry both types permanently rather than being
genuinely reclassified.

ADOPTED PATTERN (ETL, non-monotonic by design):
WHERE ?rc isAccepted true, ETL:
  1. Mints a new UserStory individual (new issueId/issueKey)
  2. Asserts: newStory arto:supersedes ?rc
  3. Leaves ?rc&apos;s rdf:type and all pre-acceptance trace links untouched

This gives clean, non-monotonic reclassification semantics (the
promoted requirement genuinely &apos;becomes&apos; a UserStory going forward)
while keeping RequirementCandidate/UserStory disjointness — and every
structural metric in Chapter 8 that depends on it — fully intact.

CQ-PROMO SPARQL (promotion history):
SELECT ?candidate ?candidateType ?promoted WHERE {
  ?promoted a arto:UserStory .
  ?promoted arto:supersedes ?candidate .
  ?candidate a ?candidateType .
  ?candidateType rdfs:subClassOf* arto:RequirementCandidate .
}

Pilot verification: story_004 arto:supersedes suggestion_002 ;
suggestion_002 a arto:Suggestion ; suggestion_002 arto:isAccepted true.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#ProblemTicket -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;ProblemTicket">
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="&arto;Investigation"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#Question -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;Question"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#R1_TransitiveImpact -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;R1_TransitiveImpact">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">R1 — Impact Inference</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SWRL Rule R1 — Impact Inference (CQ4)
Executable as R1a–R1e (swrl:Imp at the end of this file).

Rules view syntax:
UserStory(?s) ^ hasImplementingTask(?s, ?t) ^ SprintTask(?t) -&gt; impacts(?s, ?t)
UserStory(?s) ^ hasImplementingTask(?s, ?t) ^ tracesTo(?t, ?c) ^ CodeCommit(?c) -&gt; impacts(?s, ?c)
Bug(?b) ^ reportedIn(?b, ?s) ^ UserStory(?s) -&gt; impacts(?b, ?s)
Bug(?b) ^ causes(?b, ?b2) ^ Bug(?b2) -&gt; impacts(?b, ?b2)
Bug(?b) ^ blocks(?b, ?s) ^ UserStory(?s) -&gt; impacts(?b, ?s)   [R1e, added Nov 2026]

Explanation:
- Rule fires on all UserStory individuals with hasImplementingTask assertions
- Infers impacts from UserStory to SprintTask and transitively to CodeCommit
- Bug causation chains are also captured via causes property
- impacts is declared Transitive so HermiT extends chains automatically
- All inferred impacts count as hasTraceLink via SubPropertyOf declaration
- An ETL post-processing step is designed to record inferred links
  as InferredLink individuals (link_005 in the pilot shows the form;
  it is asserted pilot data, not reasoner output)
- SPARQL in Protégé 4.3 reads asserted triples only, so the query
  below returns asserted impacts; inferred ones show in the
  Individuals tab after HermiT runs

CQ4 SPARQL:
SELECT ?s ?impacted WHERE {
  ?s a arto:UserStory .
  ?s arto:impacts ?impacted .
}</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#R2_TestCoverageInference -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;R2_TestCoverageInference">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">R2 — Test Coverage Inference</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SWRL Rule R2 — Test Coverage Inference (CQ3/CQ5)
Executable as R2a–R2b (swrl:Imp at the end of this file).

Rules view syntax:
TestCase(?tc) ^ verifies(?tc, ?s) ^ UserStory(?s) -&gt; hasTraceLink(?s, ?tc)
TestCase(?tc) ^ verifies(?tc, ?b) ^ Bug(?b) -&gt; hasTraceLink(?b, ?tc)

Explanation:
- Ensures test-story links appear in hasTraceLink coverage queries
- Without this rule, verifies assertions exist but story_001 may not
  appear in hasTraceLink-based orphan detection
- The inverse direction (story hasTraceLink testcase) is needed for
  CQ5 to correctly exclude verified stories from OrphanArtefact
- Creates InferredLink with:
    assertionMethod = SWRL
    hasLinkType = arto:DesignLink_Type
    isInferred = true
    sdlcLinkDirection = CrossCutting

CQ3a SPARQL:
SELECT ?tc ?story WHERE {
  ?tc a arto:TestCase .
  ?tc arto:verifies ?story .
  ?story a arto:UserStory .
}

CQ3b SPARQL (stories with no test coverage):
SELECT ?story WHERE {
  ?story a arto:UserStory .
  MINUS { ?tc arto:verifies ?story . }
}</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#R3_SemanticEquivalencePropagation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;R3_SemanticEquivalencePropagation">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">R3 — Semantic Equivalence Propagation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SWRL Rule R3 — Semantic Equivalence Propagation (CQ8)
Executable as R3a–R3c in arto-m4-semantic.ttl. Documentation only here.

R3a: AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
     skos:exactMatch(?v1, ?v2) ^ hasTraceLink(?v1, ?l) -&gt; hasTraceLink(?v2, ?l)
R3b: AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
     skos:exactMatch(?v1, ?v2) ^ hasTraceLink(?v2, ?l) -&gt; hasTraceLink(?v1, ?l)
R3c: AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
     skos:exactMatch(?v1, ?v2) ^ impacts(?v1, ?t) -&gt; impacts(?v2, ?t)

Explanation:
- Fires when two artefacts are declared skos:exactMatch (synonyms)
- R3b is required: SKOS is not imported and exactMatch is not declared
  symmetric, so the reasoner does not infer the reverse of a pair
- skos:exactMatch must be an object property (declared in M1 Step 5,
  M4 and the pilot) or SWRL cannot use it
- Verified on the pilot: story_equiv and bug_equiv receive the trace
  and impacts links of story_001 and bug_001 with HermiT active

CQ8 SPARQL:
SELECT ?v1 ?v2 ?link WHERE {
  ?v1 skos:exactMatch ?v2 .
  ?v1 arto:hasTraceLink ?link .
  ?v2 arto:hasTraceLink ?link .
}</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#R3_SemanticEquivalencePropagation_M4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;R3_SemanticEquivalencePropagation_M4">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">R3 — Semantic Equivalence Propagation (M4 full)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SWRL Rule R3 — Full implementation in M4 (CQ8)

Rules view syntax (all three are encoded as swrl:Imp in this file):

Rule R3a — Forward propagation:
AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
skos:exactMatch(?v1, ?v2) ^ hasTraceLink(?v1, ?l)
-&gt; hasTraceLink(?v2, ?l)

Rule R3b — Backward propagation (symmetric):
AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
skos:exactMatch(?v1, ?v2) ^ hasTraceLink(?v2, ?l)
-&gt; hasTraceLink(?v1, ?l)

Rule R3c — Impact propagation across synonyms:
AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
skos:exactMatch(?v1, ?v2) ^ impacts(?v1, ?t)
-&gt; impacts(?v2, ?t)

Explanation:
- Fires when two AgileArtefact individuals are declared
  skos:exactMatch (confirmed synonyms)
- Propagates hasTraceLink and impacts assertions bidirectionally
- Example: if story_001 (Project A: &apos;Login Story&apos;) is exactMatch
  story_equiv (Project B: &apos;Authentication Story&apos;), then all
  trace links of story_001 also apply to story_equiv
- Requires TermVariant individuals with skos:exactMatch assertions
- Creates InferredLink individuals in ETL post-processing:
    assertionMethod = SWRL
    hasLinkType = AssociativeLink_Type
    isInferred = true
    sdlcLinkDirection = Horizontal

CQ8 SPARQL:
SELECT ?v1 ?v2 ?link WHERE {
  ?v1 skos:exactMatch ?v2 .
  ?v1 arto:hasTraceLink ?link .
  ?v2 arto:hasTraceLink ?link .
}

Note: the SKOS Reference makes skos:exactMatch symmetric, but SKOS
is not imported and ARTO does not redeclare symmetry. Pilot data
asserts each exactMatch pair in one direction only, so R3b is
required for links to flow in both directions.

Verification: run HermiT, then inspect story_001 in the
Individuals tab. Inferred hasTraceLink values appear highlighted.
SPARQL in the embedded engine shows asserted triples only, so it
cannot confirm rule output.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#R4_OrphanArtefactClassification -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;R4_OrphanArtefactClassification">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">R4 — OrphanArtefact Classification</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">R4 — OrphanArtefact Classification (CQ5) — documentation only

R4 is not loaded as a rule. Orphan detection needs negation
(no hasTraceLink), which a Horn rule cannot express. An earlier
placeholder, AgileArtefact(?a) ^ hasTraceLink(?a, ?l) -&gt; hasTraceLink(?a, ?l),
restated its own premise and inferred nothing; it has been removed.

OrphanArtefact is defined in M1 Step 2 (two-way):
  OrphanArtefact ≡ AgileArtefact ⊓ ¬∃hasTraceLink.⊤ ⊓ ¬∃hasTraceLink⁻.⊤
Under the open world assumption HermiT never classifies a populated
individual into it.

CQ5 is answered by SPARQL MINUS (closed world), checking both
directions:
SELECT ?artefact WHERE {
  ?artefact a ?type .
  ?type rdfs:subClassOf* arto:AgileArtefact .
  MINUS { ?artefact arto:hasTraceLink ?out . }
  MINUS { ?in arto:hasTraceLink ?artefact . }
}
Note: the embedded engine reads asserted triples only, so links that
exist only through inference (sub-property, R2, R3) do not exclude
an artefact from this result.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#S7ReuseDocumentation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;S7ReuseDocumentation">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">S7 ODP Reuse Documentation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">S7 CONTENT ODP REUSE — Conceptual Instantiation Level

PART-WHOLE CONTENT ODP:
  Source: http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/partof.owl
  ARTO instantiation:
    arto:hasPart / arto:isPartOf follow Part-Whole ODP pattern
    arto:AgileArtefact plays both Part and Whole roles
    rdfs:isDefinedBy declared on hasPart in arto-m1-step4.ttl
  Why owl:imports not used:
    Importing partof.owl would introduce odp:Part and odp:Whole
    classes alongside ARTO&apos;s existing hierarchy, requiring
    owl:equivalentProperty between odp:hasPart and arto:hasPart.
    This adds axioms that provide no additional CQ coverage
    and clutters the Protégé class hierarchy with unused ODP
    template classes. Level 1 (conceptual instantiation with
    rdfs:isDefinedBy) is the standard in published ontology
    engineering practice and fully satisfies the NeOn S7 scenario.

EVENT CONTENT ODP:
  Source: http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/
          timeindexedsituation.owl
  ARTO instantiation:
    arto:Sprint rdfs:subClassOf arto:Event
    arto:Event provides hasEventStatus; the pattern&apos;s time interval is realised by
    Sprint&apos;s startDate / endDate data properties
    rdfs:isDefinedBy declared on Sprint in arto-m1-step4.ttl
  Why owl:imports not used:
    Same rationale as Part-Whole. The Event ODP defines
    Event, TimeInterval, Object, and Situation as interlinked
    classes — importing these would require mapping each to
    ARTO equivalents (Sprint↔Event, startDate↔TimeInterval)
    without adding CQ coverage. The conceptual pattern is
    followed and cited; formal import is not required.

THESIS CLAIM:
  S7 executed at conceptual instantiation level — the standard
  form of ODP reuse in published ontology engineering. Both ODPs
  are cited via rdfs:isDefinedBy in the relevant module files.
  This satisfies the NeOn S7 scenario requirement that ODP
  patterns are applied and their sources are formally attributed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#SDLCPhaseLookup -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;SDLCPhaseLookup">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SDLC Phase Lookup Table</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ETL lookup table for sdlcLinkDirection calculation:

ARTEFACT CLASS → SDLC PHASE:
  Epic, UserStory, RequirementCandidate,
  Suggestion, Improvement, NewFeature     → Requirements
  ArchitectureDocument, DesignModel,
  Prototype                               → Design
  SprintTask, CodeCommit                  → Implementation
  TestCase, TestResult                    → Testing
  Version, PlannedRelease                 → Deployment
  Bug, Documentation, SupportRequest,
  BuildFailure, ProblemTicket             → Maintenance

SDLC DIRECTION RULES:
  sourcePhase == targetPhase              → Horizontal
  sourcePhase precedes targetPhase        → Forward
  sourcePhase follows targetPhase         → Backward
  phases are non-adjacent (skip ≥1)      → CrossCutting

PHASE ORDER: Requirements &lt; Design &lt; Implementation
             &lt; Testing &lt; Deployment &lt; Maintenance

EXAMPLES:
  UserStory → SprintTask:  Requirements→Implementation = Forward
  Bug → UserStory:         Maintenance→Requirements    = Backward
  TestCase → UserStory:    Testing→Requirements        = CrossCutting
  Bug → Bug:               Maintenance→Maintenance     = Horizontal</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ub.bw/ontologies/arto#SWRLRegistry -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&arto;SWRLRegistry">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ARTO SWRL Rules Registry</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ARTO SWRL Rules — registry (documentation)

EXECUTION: the rules are encoded as swrl:Imp in the module files and
load automatically into Protégé 4.3&apos;s Rules view
(Window → Views → Ontology views → Rules). They are DL-safe, so
HermiT applies them during reasoning; no separate rule engine is
used. 10 executable rules in total: R1a–R1e and R2a–R2b in M2,
R3a–R3c in M4. Inferred values appear in the Individuals tab;
Protégé&apos;s SPARQL engine reads asserted triples only.

R1 — Impact Inference (CQ4) [M2] — R1a–R1e:
Not itself a transitivity rule: chaining comes from impacts being
owl:TransitiveProperty.
UserStory(?s) ^ hasImplementingTask(?s,?t) ^ SprintTask(?t)
  -&gt; impacts(?s,?t)
UserStory(?s) ^ hasImplementingTask(?s,?t) ^ tracesTo(?t,?c)
  ^ CodeCommit(?c) -&gt; impacts(?s,?c)
Bug(?b) ^ reportedIn(?b,?s) ^ UserStory(?s)
  -&gt; impacts(?b,?s)
Bug(?b) ^ causes(?b,?b2) ^ Bug(?b2)
  -&gt; impacts(?b,?b2)
Bug(?b) ^ blocks(?b,?s) ^ UserStory(?s)
  -&gt; impacts(?b,?s)            [R1e]
reportedIn has no TAWOS source, so R1c fires on the pilot only.

R2 — Test Coverage Inference (CQ3/CQ5) [M2] — R2a–R2b:
TestCase(?tc) ^ verifies(?tc,?s) ^ UserStory(?s)
  -&gt; hasTraceLink(?s,?tc)
TestCase(?tc) ^ verifies(?tc,?b) ^ Bug(?b)
  -&gt; hasTraceLink(?b,?tc)

R3 — Semantic Equivalence Propagation (CQ8) [M4] — R3a–R3c:
R3a: AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
     skos:exactMatch(?v1,?v2) ^ hasTraceLink(?v1,?l)
     -&gt; hasTraceLink(?v2,?l)
R3b: AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
     skos:exactMatch(?v1,?v2) ^ hasTraceLink(?v2,?l)
     -&gt; hasTraceLink(?v1,?l)
R3c: AgileArtefact(?v1) ^ AgileArtefact(?v2) ^
     skos:exactMatch(?v1,?v2) ^ impacts(?v1,?t)
     -&gt; impacts(?v2,?t)
R3b is required: SKOS is not imported and exactMatch is not declared
symmetric, so the reasoner does not infer the reverse of a pair.

R4 — OrphanArtefact Classification (CQ5) — documentation only:
Not a rule. Orphan detection needs negation, which SWRL cannot express.
OrphanArtefact is defined in M1 Step 2 (two-way):
  OrphanArtefact ≡ AgileArtefact ⊓ ¬∃hasTraceLink.⊤ ⊓ ¬∃hasTraceLink⁻.⊤
Under the open world assumption HermiT never classifies a populated
individual into it. CQ5 is answered by SPARQL MINUS (closed world),
checking both directions:
  SELECT ?a WHERE {
    ?a a ?type .
    ?type rdfs:subClassOf* arto:AgileArtefact .
    MINUS { ?a arto:hasTraceLink ?out . }
    MINUS { ?in arto:hasTraceLink ?a . }
  }</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


